Category: Knowledge Compression
Purpose:
  Defines the knowledge compression pipeline that transforms
  raw observations into canonical knowledge. Prevents knowledge
  dump by enforcing semantic clustering and normalization.

Owns: ./

Compression Pipeline:

  CODE
    ↓
  OBSERVATIONS
    ↓
  CONCEPT EXTRACTION
    ↓
  SEMANTIC CLUSTERING
    ↓
  CANONICALIZATION
    ↓
  RELATION DETECTION
    ↓
  REFERENCE CREATION

  Input: raw observations from code analysis, tasks, decisions.
  Output: minimal set of canonical concepts with typed relations.

  Example:
    20 observations
      ↓
    semantic clustering
      ↓
    1 concept
      ↓
    3 contextual rules

Three Knowledge Levels:

  Concept   — What is it? (@concept.idempotency)
  Rule      — How applied in our project? (@payment.idempotency)
  Skill     — How do we implement it? (@skill.idempotent-command)

  These three MUST NOT be conflated.

Knowledge Extraction Rules:
  [K1] AI MUST search for existing concepts before creating new ones.
  [K2] AI MUST cluster semantically similar observations.
  [K3] AI MUST canonicalize to preferred terminology.
  [K4] AI MUST detect and declare relations between concepts.
  [K5] AI MUST produce contextual rules, not generic statements.

Knowledge Diff Format:

  When comparing current knowledge vs observed project state:

  + <concept>     — NEW: exists in project, not in knowledge
  ~ <concept>     — CHANGED: exists in both, definition differs
  - <concept>     — REMOVED: in knowledge, no longer in project
  ! <concept>     — CONFLICT: contradicts existing knowledge
  ? <concept>     — UNKNOWN: cannot determine status

  Example:
    + @skill.idempotent-command
    ~ @architecture.event-driven
    - @candidate.old-retry-pattern
    ! @decision.transaction-boundary

  Diff Categories:
    NEW:       knowledge gap, needs candidate creation
    CHANGED:   knowledge drift, needs version bump
    REMOVED:   orphaned knowledge, needs archival
    CONFLICT:  contradiction, needs human resolution
    UNKNOWN:   insufficient evidence, needs investigation

Knowledge Locality:

  Tasks do NOT require the entire knowledge graph.
  AI loads only relevant nodes based on task context.

  Task: @task.withdraw
    Relevant:     @payment, @wallet, @transaction, @aggregate, @idempotency
    Not loaded:   @frontend.animation, @marketing, @analytics.dashboard

  Locality Rules:
    [L1] Start with task's direct references (radius 1).
    [L2] Expand to radius 2 only when context is insufficient.
    [L3] always_load nodes are always included regardless of task.
    [L4] Loading stops when context confidence is sufficient.

Reference Radius:

  radius = 1  — direct references (task → skill)
  radius = 2  — references of references (skill → concept)
  radius = 3  — full chain (concept → decision → code → test)

  Default: 1 → 2
  Maximum: 3 (on-demand only)

